        "text": "ink",
        "contrast": 7.63
      },
      "cpu": {
        "text": "ink",
        "contrast": 5.13
      }
    },
    "rules": [
      "Every port-coloured element also carries its port number (P1-P4, or CPU) from strings, so colour is never the only cue.",
      "Port colours are never used for selection; selection is gold plus the lift-and-plate motion.",
      "P3 yellow and the selection gold sit close under red-green colour blindness (see checks.port_vs_gold); the number and the plate extrusion carry the difference."
    ]
  },
  "type": {
    "fonts": {
      "sans": {
        "name": "Source Sans 3",
        "licence": "SIL OFL 1.1",
        "files": {
          "bold": "SourceSans3/SourceSans3-Bold.otf",
          "black": "SourceSans3/SourceSans3-Black.otf"
        }
      },
      "mono": {
        "name": "Hasklug Nerd Font (Hasklig)",
        "licence": "SIL OFL 1.1",
        "files": {
          "bold": "Hasklug/HasklugNerdFont-Bold.otf",
          "black": "Hasklug/HasklugNerdFont-Black.otf"
        }
      }
    },
    "scale": [
      {
        "role": "caption",
        "size": 12,
        "face": "sans",
        "weight": "bold",
        "charset": "full",
        "use": "badges, section-divider labels, table footnotes; the smallest size allowed"
      },
      {
        "role": "body",
        "size": 14,
        "face": "sans",
        "weight": "bold",
        "charset": "full",
        "use": "descriptions, footer hints, dialog body, breadcrumb, table cells, character names on player panels"
      },
      {
        "role": "row",
        "size": 16,
        "face": "sans",
        "weight": "black",
        "charset": "full",
        "use": "list rows and widget values, stage name plate"
      },
      {
        "role": "label",
        "size": 20,
        "face": "sans",
        "weight": "black",
        "charset": "full",
        "use": "secondary hub tiles, dialog buttons"
      },
      {
        "role": "title",
        "size": 24,
        "face": "sans",
        "weight": "black",
        "charset": "full",
        "use": "header titles, dialog titles, ordinal suffixes"
      },
      {
        "role": "heading",
        "size": 32,
        "face": "sans",
        "weight": "black",
        "charset": "full",
        "use": "panel headings, banners"
      },
      {
        "role": "hero",
        "size": 44,
        "face": "sans",
        "weight": "black",
        "charset": "caps",
        "use": "hero tile labels (always set in capitals)"
      },
      {
        "role": "display",
        "size": 56,
        "face": "sans",
        "weight": "black",
        "charset": "caps",
        "use": "placement numerals, READY banner"
      },
      {
        "role": "tag",
        "size": 20,
        "face": "mono",
        "weight": "black",
        "charset": "full",
        "use": "name tags and the name-entry field: 4 fixed-width cells, so the caret and the plate never move as letters change"
      },
      {
        "role": "code",
        "size": 16,
        "face": "mono",
        "weight": "bold",
        "charset": "code",
        "use": "network codes and addresses (code plate): max 21 characters, 255.255.255.255:65535 = 201.6 px"
      }
    ],
    "choice": {
      "proportional": {
        "face": "sans",
        "why": [
          "Hasklug is monospaced (0.6 em a cell), so a 20-character name at body size is 168 px against a 136 px portrait; proportional Source Sans 3 sets the longest vanilla name, 'Mr. Game & Watch', in 110.5 px.",
          "Same designer and skeleton as Source Code Pro, which Hasklig is built on: the two faces share letter shapes and weights, so the switch between them does not show.",
          "SIL OFL 1.1 (licence text in SourceSans3/LICENSE.md, files from Adobe's official 3.052R release). Its CJK companion, Source Han Sans, is also OFL - the second-script pages can come from the same family.",
          "Its default figures are tabular (540 units in Black), so numbers and stats do not need a separate monospaced face; font_atlas.py checks digits in every role."
        ]
      },
      "monospaced": {
        "face": "mono",
        "roles": [
          "tag",
          "code"
        ],
        "why": [
          "Only where fixed cells are the point: the 4-character name tag and name entry (the caret and plate never move), and network codes (digits line up, and a code that changes never shifts the copy icon; the zero is dotted)."
        ]
      }
    },
    "names": {
      "plate_1x": 136,
      "pad_1x": 6,
      "roles": [
        "body",
        "caption"
      ],
      "max_chars": 20,
      "rule": "Set in body; if wider than plate - 2*pad, caption; if still wider, truncate with '…'. font_atlas.py checks the 20-character test names below.",
      "test_names": [
        "Mr. Game & Watch Jr.",
        "Captain Falcon Alt 2",
        "Princess Daisy (SSB)",
        "Dark Samus & Metroid",
        "Wario Man, Microgame",
        "Young Link (Classic)"
      ]
    },
    "fit": [
      "Slots are sized in px (max_width_1x); a character count is only a guide for proportional text.",
      "If a string is wider than its slot: set it one role smaller (same face); if still too wide, truncate with '…'. Never squash horizontally."
    ],
    "min_size": 12,
    "italic": {
      "method": "shear glyph quads",
      "S": 0.25,
      "formula": "x' = x + (baseline_y - y) * S"
    },
    "ordinal": {
      "numeral": "display",
      "suffix": "title",
      "align": "suffix cap top = numeral cap top",
      "suffixes": [
        "st",
        "nd",
        "rd",
        "th"
      ]
    },
    "charsets": {
      "full": "printable ASCII 0x20-0x7E + extras",
      "caps": "ASCII without a-z + extras; engine uppercases hero/display text",
      "code": "network codes only:  -.0123456789:?[]ABCDEFabcdefx… (anything else -> '?')",
      "extras": "×%°…–—←→↑↓★"
    }
  },
